/-!
# The pull-salvo generator with a continue glider

A fan-out placed in front of the generator `pullGenerator` (research note `N-15`): one control
glider makes the assembly emit the pulling salvo **and** a further glider, the *continue glider*,
which can trigger the next component of a machine. The design was found by the project's own
search (`scripts/life_machine`, report `notes/research/reports/R-22-push-and-continue.md`,
design `CG1`).

* `fanOut`: two blocked pairs of guns (four guns), periodic with period 30
  (`fanOut_evolve_thirty`).
* `fanOut_reaction`: with the control glider `cgControl`, in 840 generations the fan-out emits
  the control glider of `pullGenerator` (`pullGeneratorControl`, at exactly the right place and
  time) and the continue glider `contStart`, and is back in its cycle; certified in seven parts,
  inside the box `-187 ≤ x ≤ 34`, `-225 ≤ y ≤ -7`.
* `continueGenerator_reaction`: the whole assembly `pullGenerator ∪ fanOut` with `cgControl`
  evolves in 2010 generations into itself, the pulling salvo `translate (51, 143) pullSalvo` and
  the continue glider `contEnd`, staying in the box `-479 ≤ x ≤ 90`, `-225 ≤ y ≤ 179`.

The proof is compositional: the fan-out's reaction runs beside the generator at rest (their
boxes are seven rows apart); then `pullGenerator_reaction` runs beside the fan-out at rest and
the continue glider in flight (`reaction_flight_box'`, a moving box). Only the fan-out's reaction
is a new certificate.

**Sanity.** `fanOut_evolve_thirty` (without control the fan-out emits nothing),
`contStart_evolve_four` (the continue glider is a glider travelling down and to the left).
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace LeanTheory.Life

open Finset

/-! ### Tools -/

/-- Being far apart from two sets is being far apart from their union. -/
theorem FarApart.union_right {r : ℕ} {A B C : Set Cell} (h₁ : FarApart r A B)
    (h₂ : FarApart r A C) : FarApart r A (B ∪ C) :=
  fun a ha x hx => hx.elim (h₁ a ha x) (h₂ a ha x)

/-- **Flight for any number of generations**: a pattern that reappears translated by `v` after
`p > 0` generations, and stays in a box during its first `p` generations, stays at every time
`i` in that box moved by `(i / p) • v`. -/
theorem reaction_flight_box' {S : Finset Cell} {p : ℕ} {v : Cell} {a b lo hi : ℤ} (hp : 0 < p)
    (hS : conway.evolve p S = translate v S)
    (hB : ∀ r < p, (conway.evolve r S : Set Cell) ⊆ Box a b lo hi) (n : ℕ) :
    Reaction S (conway.evolve n S) n
      (fun i => (fun c => (i / p) • v + c) '' Box a b lo hi) := by
  refine ⟨rfl, fun i _ c hc => ?_⟩
  rw [mem_coe, evolve_eq_translate_mod hS, mem_translate] at hc
  exact ⟨c - (i / p) • v, hB _ (Nat.mod_lt _ hp) (mem_coe.2 hc), by simp⟩

/-- Rearranging a union of four configurations. -/
theorem union_rearrange (A B C D : Finset Cell) : A ∪ (B ∪ C ∪ D) = A ∪ C ∪ (B ∪ D) := by
  ext c
  simp only [mem_union]
  tauto

